  "selection": "For every candidate make exactly one inner OOF continuous prediction per outer-training wine. Optimize pooled six-class Macro F1 over five ordered cutpoints. Rank threshold candidates by this FITTED threshold-training objective; it is not an unbiased inner performance estimate. Rank rounding candidates by pooled OOF Macro F1 at fixed half-integer cuts. Exact ties use fixed candidate order; no outer scores or supporting metrics select.",
  "outer_refits": "Refit the threshold-selected and rounding-selected configurations once each on all outer training, reusing the fit if identical. Freeze all learned cutpoints before outer prediction. Matched rounding applies naive cuts to the threshold-selected continuous predictions.",
  "joint_selection": "Within each outer training split choose the highest inner threshold objective across all24 candidates, and separately the highest rounding OOF objective. Reuse matching family results; joint matched rounding uses the joint threshold-selected regressor. No new fits or outer-based family selection.",
  "threshold_method": "Dynamic programming globally maximizes floating-point Macro F1 over every contiguous partition of distinct OOF scores. Equal scores cannot split; empty predicted classes allowed. Lowest-predecessor ties. Exact rational cutpoints placed inside gaps, including repeated cut ranks, are strictly ordered and serialized losslessly. Labels use exact comparisons; float cutpoints are for display only.",
  "naive_rule": "Fixed half-integer cuts [3.5,4.5,5.5,6.5,7.5], equality enters upper class, extremes map to3/8. No bankers rounding.",
